:db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341308/field-3/cc6744f8d99f3b1f7e72cc930221acf54df3d62bd21b63e469b40b1a86f013bb" :answer/id #uuid "c6d6a061-82e9-5419-b645-6416c417ab5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341308/field-3/85f419139c3932e1f4939f3dda2f61e0be06a7afe61eaf1d863582a15ba53de4" :answer/id #uuid "cbb694a7-a617-506d-9ab1-ca50bd0c2025" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341308/field-3/dc9cafd927906d4e6d622eca6b2d98f3e54440fda6f53f8615fa398e6253aa9a" :answer/id #uuid "15574010-dde5-541c-8696-8092880f5861" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341308/field-3/00cf2981dc86733a603826a01923a100ca9761048843c165757d3bb8a288c81e" :answer/id #uuid "9b980876-cfc5-575a-8d21-f2589457115b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341308/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b9948c1-dc39-5af2-a50a-28c98d07a5c5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-341308/field-3/dc9cafd927906d4e6d622eca6b2d98f3e54440fda6f53f8615fa398e6253aa9a" :answer-field/choices ["q-341308/field-3/67554054b12d5aba305b18db51e56ab64e5990c3dbb57596462cb1db6c6e380f" "q-341308/field-3/cc6744f8d99f3b1f7e72cc930221acf54df3d62bd21b63e469b40b1a86f013bb" "q-341308/field-3/85f419139c3932e1f4939f3dda2f61e0be06a7afe61eaf1d863582a15ba53de4" "q-341308/field-3/dc9cafd927906d4e6d622eca6b2d98f3e54440fda6f53f8615fa398e6253aa9a" "q-341308/field-3/00cf2981dc86733a603826a01923a100ca9761048843c165757d3bb8a288c81e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341308" :question/id #uuid "73b220ad-78ed-5227-b775-ed2065f7b0fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-341308" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=3x+1$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{0}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),1⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),1⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),1⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨1,1⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x]}_{-0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),1⟩ & =\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩ \\\\ {a}_{0} & =\\frac{2⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩} \\\\ {a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341308/field-1" "q-341308/field-2" "q-341308/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "304c015d-cbb6-5989-a102-d6f0f5f38604"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341308"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341309/field-1/ee8f51f8de97c712111243f989ef2929bd14a15753480d316a98ef9da4ecc1ca" :answer/id #uuid "deedd464-fc68-5869-9666-3733a67c2d38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341309/field-1/3f4ac37971f00eead06694aa71f9cbcfaf9065005c7cf75ed97a13a90356ff24" :answer/id #uuid "20d89d5f-2371-5a24-9f90-495096655254" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341309/field-1/808fa46739c1202a0150843e269951816b496dece9704c17e07f1f61b9a5f26f" :answer/id #uuid "024863c6-206f-53d2-a893-328f932cfd4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341309/field-1/f7403f6eb802785afdec6495efd96521e1f3f038e252c23af16c3565311efdc0" :answer/id #uuid "a3124ac3-caa5-5098-a316-a30d9e731003" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{⟨1,1⟩}{⟨f(x),1⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341309/field-1/01ead8253f26db744369c0ee0a10ccde3064b560f7d8dbf95f0e2151f8586fd1" :answer/id #uuid "d11c1c1e-183e-5ad8-8fc5-6f85b3edff0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{c