r/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341309/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "36dcd912-bde9-56f4-aa8d-64e92b01a1e4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-341309/field-2/b70aae751b2c8b3e9e8a13d794a4d2996d95172e6176a2e8db9c2f456750b489" :answer-field/choices ["q-341309/field-2/b70aae751b2c8b3e9e8a13d794a4d2996d95172e6176a2e8db9c2f456750b489" "q-341309/field-2/167ebf11c001034e2cbb5c82fd03c6c789b33fae94a34649b1567e72676329e0" "q-341309/field-2/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-341309/field-2/a319e2074b264fdb964c2b6eb43d32d763280e23b0599a55d545f0a58e6fea9e" "q-341309/field-2/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341309/field-3/8587caaa6759ea2d7c4855c11705a2008658cba03cecda43e18bd211b8808999" :answer/id #uuid "f9db71a0-01bd-56f9-92f8-fad491d7eff1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341309/field-3/84322203bb521ea40ae60b408b8eaa9475fdd62903b1b68521890666fe213a45" :answer/id #uuid "6025c190-b387-58a1-bdef-2bb2d224904c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341309/field-3/89836040bd9f8a870c3d50b88e5e444b7f714d5d932096c9e843b0cf7d575003" :answer/id #uuid "30c62446-e043-509e-9841-e65d9d81b96d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341309/field-3/580c620c48c9b2995f20a5a45bcfdc597482123a40446e7241ab53a89e3d9efa" :answer/id #uuid "0f0f8bf5-16cf-5f6d-90d8-bb48905065b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341309/field-3/124d8dece0d6d42fda84e985532393e2561df1b6e4dcbca069923fab1eaf675d" :answer/id #uuid "b9b05ed7-99f2-5fe1-8b6a-eff8132536b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341309/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9e59ffb-76e1-57e9-a613-63f711dd7840" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-341309/field-3/8587caaa6759ea2d7c4855c11705a2008658cba03cecda43e18bd211b8808999" :answer-field/choices ["q-341309/field-3/8587caaa6759ea2d7c4855c11705a2008658cba03cecda43e18bd211b8808999" "q-341309/field-3/84322203bb521ea40ae60b408b8eaa9475fdd62903b1b68521890666fe213a45" "q-341309/field-3/89836040bd9f8a870c3d50b88e5e444b7f714d5d932096c9e843b0cf7d575003" "q-341309/field-3/580c620c48c9b2995f20a5a45bcfdc597482123a40446e7241ab53a89e3d9efa" "q-341309/field-3/124d8dece0d6d42fda84e985532393e2561df1b6e4dcbca069923fab1eaf675d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341309" :question/id #uuid "6dd6bd1a-c741-5e2c-88f0-b51905cb07d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-341309" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{0}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),1⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),1⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),1⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨1,1⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),1⟩ & =\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩ \\\\ {a}_{0} & =\\frac{2⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩} \\\\ {a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341309/field-1" "q-341309/field-2" "q-341309/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "304c015d-cbb6-5989-a102-d6f0f5f38604"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341309"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
